@startuml seq-savestate-epoch
title Savestate / loadstate and the epoch resync contract

actor "User" as U
participant "ares" as A
participant "NetPak glue" as GL
participant "DeviceCore" as D
participant "NetClient" as N
participant "Game (via libnetpak)" as G
participant "Peer game" as P

== save ==
U -> A : savestate
A -> GL : serialize(s)
GL -> D : serialize: blob ver, registers,\nRX ring (indices+contents), TX slot,\ncommand FSM, epoch; + irqLine
note over D,N : relay session (token, socket)\ndeliberately NOT serialized -\nit lives in NetClient

== load ==
U -> A : loadstate
A -> GL : unserialize(s)
GL -> D : restore state
GL -> D : epoch++
GL -> N : requestFlush()  // drop stale in-flight frames
GL -> GL : recompute IRQ line
note right of N : session survived in real time;\npeers kept playing while we\nwere "in the past"

== game-level resync ==
G -> G : per-frame: netpak_epoch() changed!
G -> P : app-level resync (ch1):\nrequest state snapshot / rejoin lockstep
P --> G : current game state
note over G,P : the device converts an emulator\nanomaly into an ordinary netcode\nevent games already handle
@enduml
